{"title":"2025 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 16","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/3/d037f1aa313d30fe7ade693f1b672ed2a68880fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$34$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> students, including Pedro and Hwie-Lie, are sitting side-by-side in a row of chairs. Pedro counted <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/1/9a1b2497e7b125cd721bab4c6e2385f954fe35cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$23$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> students, including Hwie-Lie, to his left. Hwie-Lie counted <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> students, including Pedro, to her right. How many students are seated between Pedro and Hwie-Lie?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/5/c35bbe96fdd447778e0f642371b208bcce7b616f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ 4 \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ 2 \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 8 \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ 11 \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ 15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"406\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> be the number of people that are seated between the two. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/1/9a1b2497e7b125cd721bab4c6e2385f954fe35cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$23$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> students are on the left of Pedro and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> students to the right of Hwie-Lie, so there would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/b/0abf5017554a3250504e1b2cb06fe65c26689905.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$23 + 15 = 38$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"103\" height=\"15\" /> students, counting the people who are seated between the two.\n</p><p>This means that we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/a/71ae52366444a09611b6415a3eacac487d94294b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$38 - x = 34$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"95\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/5/435312609d17aa5b5047d347a05bb278f665d491.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 38 - 34 = \\boxed{\\textbf {(A) } 4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"175\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 CEMC Pascal (page does not exist)\">2025 CEMC Pascal</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 CEMC Pascal Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 CEMC Pascal Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2025 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 15\">Problem 15</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2025 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 17\">Problem 17</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2025 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2025 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2025 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2025 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2025 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2025 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2025 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_8\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2025 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2025 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 9\">9</a